runtime: optional asynchronous VIF1/GIF DMA (PS2X_ASYNC_DMA=1). sceDmaSend
hands VIF1 and GIF (path 3) transfers, copied at kick time, to a DMA worker
thread that runs them in order (VIF1 unpack, VU1 programs, XGKICK) while the
EE carries on, as the real DMAC and VU1 do. The channel stays busy until the
EE sees the worker done: sceDmaSync waits (or reports busy when polling), the
scheduler polls and raises the completions with their DMAC handlers, and any
guest access to GIF/VIF/DMA/D_*/VU1/GS privileged registers, GS stub or GIF
packet from another thread waits for the worker first. Off by default.

